You are building ClearSign — an AI contract clause explainer SaaS.

STACK:
- Next.js 14 App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui
- Supabase (auth + postgres + storage)
- Google Gemini API via @google/generative-ai package
- Lemon Squeezy for payments
- pdf-parse for PDF text extraction, mammoth for DOCX extraction
- Puppeteer for PDF export of analysis
- react-dropzone for file uploads
- Vercel for hosting

DESIGN:
- Primary color: #1A3C5E (navy)
- Alert/danger color: #E8401C (orange-red)
- Font: Inter
- Mobile-first, clean, minimal UI
- Risk score 0–10 where 10 = most risky (red), 5–7 = medium (amber), 0–4 = low (green)

RULES:
- Always use App Router, never pages router
- Always use TypeScript
- Use shadcn/ui components wherever possible
- All Supabase server calls use createServerClient from @supabase/ssr
- All Supabase client calls use createBrowserClient from @supabase/ssr
- Never hardcode API keys — always use process.env
- Always handle loading, error, and empty states in UI
- Free plan limits: 5 analyses/lifetime, 3 chat questions/analysis, 3 contracts stored
- Solo plan: 25 analyses/month, unlimited chat, 50 contracts, PDF export enabled
- Pro plan: 80 analyses/month, unlimited chat, unlimited contracts, PDF export enabled
- Legal disclaimer must appear on every analysis result: "ClearSign provides AI-generated analysis for informational purposes only. This is NOT legal advice. Always consult a qualified attorney before signing any contract."
- File uploads accept: PDF, DOCX, TXT only. Max 20MB.
- No OCR, no image upload support